CORRECTED BY MISTAKE-234: return semigroups prove reachability only; mixed-sign noncancellation and the DvdK bypass remain open.

========================================================================
A  the coprime PAIR {-q,p} is PERIODIC: R = multiples of p+q (THM-1840); Frobenius = infinity
========================================================================
  S={-2,3} (coprime True): period d=5=p+q=5; R (returns) start [5, 10, 15, 20, 25, 30] = multiples of 5? True ; Frobenius=inf (periodic)
  S={-1,2} (coprime True): period d=3=p+q=3; R (returns) start [3, 6, 9, 12, 15, 18] = multiples of 3? True ; Frobenius=inf (periodic)
  S={-3,4} (coprime True): period d=7=p+q=7; R (returns) start [7, 14, 21, 28, 35, 42] = multiples of 7? True ; Frobenius=inf (periodic)
  S={-2,5} (coprime True): period d=7=p+q=7; R (returns) start [7, 14, 21, 28, 35, 42] = multiples of 7? True ; Frobenius=inf (periodic)
  => the single-character/bare-pair is fully PERIODIC: the coprime return m0=p+q, and ONLY its multiples.

========================================================================
B  the FILLED coprime interval (endpoints + interior, gcd gaps = 1) is COFINITE: R = all m >= Frob#
========================================================================
  S=[-1, 1, 2]: two-sided=True, period d=1; R starts [2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7]; Frobenius# (last non-return) = 1  => R = all m >= 2
  S=[-2, 1, 3]: two-sided=True, period d=1; R starts [3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8]; Frobenius# (last non-return) = 2  => R = all m >= 3
  S=[-2, 2, 3]: two-sided=True, period d=1; R starts [2, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8]; Frobenius# (last non-return) = 3  => R = all m >= 4
  S=[-3, -1, 1, 2]: two-sided=True, period d=1; R starts [2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7]; Frobenius# (last non-return) = 1  => R = all m >= 2
  S=[-2, -1, 1, 2, 3]: two-sided=True, period d=1; R starts [2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7]; Frobenius# (last non-return) = 1  => R = all m >= 2
  => adding INTERIOR exponents (gcd of gaps -> 1) turns the periodic pair into a COFINITE return set:
     all large m are SUPPORT returns, with a finite FROBENIUS NUMBER (the last non-return).
     This is an exact reachability characterization, not coefficient-uniform noncancellation.

========================================================================
C  POSITIVE coefficients: CT(f^m) != 0  <=>  m in R (reachability). Verified.
========================================================================
  S=[-2, 3] (coeffs=1): CT(f^m) != 0  <=>  m in R  for m=1..20 ? True  ; CT sample [0, 0, 0, 0, 10, 0, 0, 0]
  S=[-1, 1, 2] (coeffs=1): CT(f^m) != 0  <=>  m in R  for m=1..20 ? True  ; CT sample [0, 2, 3, 6, 20, 35, 105, 238]
  S=[-2, 3, 1] (coeffs=1): CT(f^m) != 0  <=>  m in R  for m=1..20 ? True  ; CT sample [0, 0, 3, 12, 10, 15, 140, 420]
  => for positive coefficients the return set R IS the nonvanishing set: the coprime-interval semigroup.

========================================================================
D  the corrected 1D support picture + the three-distance / LRC analogy
========================================================================
  ONE-DIMENSIONAL COPRIME INTERVALS -- exact SUPPORT reachability:
    interval [min S, max S]  +  period d=gcd(gaps)  =>  the RETURN SEMIGROUP R = {m : 0 in m-fold sum}.
    * bare coprime PAIR {-q,p}: PERIODIC, R = (p+q)Z_{>0}  (THM-1840 single-character seed).
    * APERIODIC two-sided support: COFINITE R, hence all m beyond a support conductor are reachable.
    * positive coeffs: CT(f^m)!=0 <=> m in R.
    * mixed/complex coeffs: a separate noncancellation theorem is required; infinitely many reachable m may vanish.
  Therefore the conductor is an effective support sidecar, not a DvdK replacement or a coefficient-uniform m0.

  THREE-DISTANCE / LRC analogy: coprimality also governs danger-arc orbit gaps. The gaps of
  {k t mod 1} take exactly THREE values (three-distance/Steinhaus), determined by the CONTINUED FRACTION of t
  = orbit arithmetic. This is a useful comparison, not a map from constant-term noncancellation to LRC.
